id: pm-fhhhlk
title: "GH-716: detect npm and Slack credential shapes in mutation secret guard"
description: "The write-time mutation secret guard misses fixed-prefix npm and Slack credential shapes, including registry authentication lines, so block mode can persist them into public item and history files. Add bounded low-false-positive detectors, keep matched values redacted from all errors and telemetry, cover advise and block modes across mutation surfaces, and document the rule inventory."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T01:00:18.735Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T01:25:59.011Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T01:24:28.976Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Npm and Slack fixed-prefix credential shapes are detected in bare, assignment, and registry-style text without storing or echoing matched values; Advise and block modes behave consistently across CLI, SDK, MCP, batch, and annotation mutation surfaces; False-positive fixtures for placeholders, hashes, package names, and ordinary prose remain allowed; Secret scan, full coverage, static security gates, and temporary public-tracker acceptance pass"
parent: pm-pim7
resolution: "Shared write-time mutation guard now detects bounded npm and Slack fixed-prefix credential shapes and returns only redacted rule/path metadata across SDK, CLI, and MCP adapters."
expected_result: "Bare, assignment, and registry-style npm/Slack credentials are detected before persistence without false positives or raw-value disclosure across mutation surfaces."
actual_result: "npm_token and slack_token rules block persistence in shared SDK guard paths; CLI/MCP advice is redacted; isolated acceptance persisted zero items; 371 files and 6401 tests pass with 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; static, docstring, duplicate, type, SDK surface, health, history, dependency-audit, and secret gates pass."
